# Rank 1716 / CVE-2018-3740: the sanitize gem's element cleaner allowlisted
# attribute names but let the values it kept reach serialization exactly as
# the parser produced them. Nokogiri is built on libxml2, and libxml2 >= 2.9.2
# deliberately leaves comment sequences unescaped inside serialized
# attributes to preserve server-side includes (libxml2 commit 960f0e27), so an
# href value carrying `<!--" onmouseover=...-->` serialises with its double
# quote intact, re-opens the attribute, and injects attributes the allowlist
# had removed (CWE-79). The fixed revision keeps the allowlist loop and additionally
# rewrites the URL-bearing values it keeps -- attr.value.strip, then
# attr.value = attr.value.gsub(/[ "]/, ' ' => '%20', '"' => '%22') on
# href/src/action everywhere and name on <a> -- so the escaped value is what
# libxml2 serialises.
#
# The weakness class is vocabulary: code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview and
# VYQL-INJ-200, whose review condition names "raw-text, comment-preservation,
# and serialization behavior" -- this is the comment-preservation case, and
# the Python, JavaScript and C# bindings for the concept had no Ruby twin.
# The Ruby binding (bindings/ruby/nokogiri_attribute_allowlist_without_
# value_rewrite.vyql) keys on Nokogiri's documented attribute API only:
# Node#attribute_nodes enumerates a node's attribute objects, Node#unlink
# (alias #remove) detaches one, and a #value read marks a pass that keeps
# attributes on their content. The discriminator is the absence of any
# value-rewrite primitive in the pass's scope -- the gsub/sub/tr families,
# Nokogiri's Node#set_attribute, and the escape/url-encode spellings -- which
# is how both sanitize's fix and loofah's CVE-2018-8048 twin
# (force_correct_attribute_escaping!, attr_node.value =
# attr_node.value.gsub(/[ "]/)) spell taking responsibility for what is kept.
# The anchor is the attribute_nodes call itself because Ruby's
# analysis.function.context statement is emitted as a sibling of the method's
# FuncDef and carries no lexical region, so scope filters over a
# function-scope presence node degrade to file scope there; the call node
# carries the method's region and confines the conjuncts to the pass.
#
# Measured on the sanitize checkout at 01629a1^ (0eee92e, vulnerable) and
# 01629a1 (fixed): 1 VYQL-INJ-200 at
# lib/sanitize/transformers/clean_element.rb:92 (the allowlist loop's
# attribute_nodes call) before, the only delta in a 33 -> 34 finding set,
# stable over three --cache off runs per side; 0 after, stable over three
# runs. The reachable set of the shape across the clones under /tmp/cve-work/
# is 13 Ruby files naming both attribute_nodes and an unlink/#remove call:
# loofah's scrub.rb clears (its own gsub), rails-html-sanitizer's scrubbers
# and open-build-service report nothing, the metasploit exploit is untouched,
# and the one collateral is Nokogiri's own
# add_child_node_and_reparent_attrs, which re-adds each removed attribute as
# node[attr_node.name] = attr_node.value -- a write the discriminator cannot
# credit, one medium review flag per Nokogiri tree, stated in the binding.
#
# The values arrive as parsed markup rather than from a labelled source, so
# this is the review direction: the flag names the pass for a caller audit,
# and the taint rules stay silent until a source reaches them.

test "rank1716: an attribute allowlist pass that never rewrites the values it keeps"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  expect VYQL-INJ-200
  expect_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  file lib/sanitize/transformers/clean_element.rb
  code
  ```
  class Sanitize; module Transformers; class CleanElement

    REGEX_DATA_ATTR = /\Adata-(?!xml)[a-z_][\w.à-öø-ſǝ-ʯ-]*\z/u

    def call(env)
      node = env[:node]
      name = env[:node_name]
      attr_whitelist = @attributes[name] || @attributes[:all]
      allow_data_attributes = attr_whitelist.include?(:data)

      node.attribute_nodes.each do |attr|
        attr_name = attr.name.downcase

        if attr_whitelist.include?(attr_name)
          if @protocols.include?(name) && @protocols[name].include?(attr_name)
            attr_protocols = @protocols[name][attr_name]

            if attr.value =~ REGEX_PROTOCOL
              attr.unlink unless attr_protocols.include?($1.downcase)
            else
              attr.unlink unless attr_protocols.include?(:relative)
            end
          end
        else
          if allow_data_attributes && attr_name.start_with?('data-')
            attr.unlink unless attr_name =~ REGEX_DATA_ATTR
          else
            attr.unlink
          end
        end
      end
    end

  end; end; end
  ```

test "rank1716: the same pass rewriting the values it keeps clears"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  reject VYQL-INJ-200
  reject_review code.HtmlSanitizerLogicReview
  file lib/sanitize/transformers/clean_element.rb
  code
  ```
  require 'set'

  class Sanitize; module Transformers; class CleanElement

    REGEX_DATA_ATTR = /\Adata-(?!xml)[a-z_][\w.à-öø-ſǝ-ʯ-]*\z/u

    UNSAFE_LIBXML_ATTRS_A = Set.new(%w[
      name
    ])

    UNSAFE_LIBXML_ATTRS_GLOBAL = Set.new(%w[
      action
      href
      src
    ])

    UNSAFE_LIBXML_ESCAPE_CHARS = {
      ' ' => '%20',
      '"' => '%22'
    }

    UNSAFE_LIBXML_ESCAPE_REGEX = /[ "]/

    def call(env)
      node = env[:node]
      name = env[:node_name]
      attr_whitelist = @attributes[name] || @attributes[:all]
      allow_data_attributes = attr_whitelist.include?(:data)

      node.attribute_nodes.each do |attr|
        attr_name = attr.name.downcase

        unless attr_whitelist.include?(attr_name)
          if allow_data_attributes && attr_name.start_with?('data-')
            next if attr_name =~ REGEX_DATA_ATTR
          end

          attr.unlink
          next
        end

        if @protocols.include?(name) && @protocols[name].include?(attr_name)
          attr_protocols = @protocols[name][attr_name]

          if attr.value =~ REGEX_PROTOCOL
            unless attr_protocols.include?($1.downcase)
              attr.unlink
              next
            end
          else
            unless attr_protocols.include?(:relative)
              attr.unlink
              next
            end
          end

          attr.value = attr.value.strip
        end

        if UNSAFE_LIBXML_ATTRS_GLOBAL.include?(attr_name) ||
            (name == 'a' && UNSAFE_LIBXML_ATTRS_A.include?(attr_name))
          attr.value = attr.value.gsub(UNSAFE_LIBXML_ESCAPE_REGEX, UNSAFE_LIBXML_ESCAPE_CHARS)
        end
      end
    end

  end; end; end
  ```
